{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"misleading-wizardly-yellowlegs","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThere is no project-wide, time-bound notice (\"Gerrit down until 14:00\", \"tracker quiet window 02:00–04:00\", \"bridge paused — heartbeat alarms expected\") that every active session sees. The canary history shows the cost: `192e-361d-24b7-42de` and `5696-5ef0-2d41-44c8` were auto-filed alarm bugs for a *deliberately paused* bridge. Banners in developer platforms converge on `message + starts_at + ends_at + severity + scope`, with expiry enforced as a read-time query filter (GitLab's stale-banner bugs came from client-side hiding), and ops tools fold the silence into the same object. Notices are advisory only in this epic — no enforcement. Consumes the inbox delivery layer [rebar:INBOX].\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd **`notice` as a first-class ticket type** with `session_log`'s carve-outs, plus typed window fields, three-seam commands, and an inbox producer.\n\n- **Type + fields**: add `\"notice\"` to `common.schema.json#/$defs/ticket_type` (`src/rebar/schemas/common.schema.json:17`) and regenerate `types.py` (`TicketType` at `src/rebar/types.py:23`; hand-add to the gate-exempt set at `types.py:75`). Four nullable state keys `notice_starts_at`, `notice_ends_at` (ns epoch strings, the store's timestamp convention), `notice_severity` (`info|warning|critical`), `notice_suppress` (list of tags), declared in `ticket_state.schema.json` and `ticket_state_llm.schema.json` exactly as `claimed_session` is (`ticket_state.schema.json:32-33`), folded from CREATE `data` by a new `_fold_notice` in `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`, updated by `EDIT` (allowlist in `src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py`) for cancel/extend, and carried in the compaction `SNAPSHOT` `compiled_state` the way `claimed_session` is. No new event type, so `KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES` is unchanged; `SCHEMA_VERSION` (`src/rebar/reducer/_version.py:41`) bumps 5→6 as a declarative projection-change record, as v5 did.\n- **Carve-outs** (every site that enumerates `session_log`, migrated in this story): hidden from default `list` (`_NON_GRAPH_ARTIFACT_TYPES`, `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:500`), from `ready` (`src/rebar/graph/_ready.py:63`) and `next-batch` (`src/rebar/_engine_support/next_batch.py:140`); rejects `blocks`/`depends_on` (graph link rules); exempt from the claim and close gates (`src/rebar/_commands/gates.py`, `_engine_support/gates.py`, `close_precheck.py`); never synced to Jira (`_engine/rebar_reconciler/config.py`, `adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py`, `outbound_differ.py`); exported by `_io/export_ndjson.py`; accepted by CLI `--type` choices and MCP models; fast-failed by plan-review claimability. Each site is classified MIGRATED or EXEMPTED (with reason) in the change description.\n- **Commands** on all three seams: `rebar notice post --until <ISO|duration> [--starts <ISO>] [--severity info|warning|critical] [--suppress <tag>]... \"<message>\"` (title = message; window validated: `ends_at > starts_at`, span ≤ 24h — a renewal cap so a fat-fingered window cannot outlive a day), `rebar notice list [--all]` (active-now by default), `rebar notice cancel <id>` (EDIT `notice_ends_at = now`), `rebar notice extend <id> --until <ISO>`; library `rebar.post_notice/list_notices/cancel_notice/extend_notice`; MCP `post_notice/list_notices/cancel_notice/extend_notice` with `notice.schema.json`.\n- **Active-now query** (single pure function `active_notices(states, now)`): `starts_at ≤ now < ends_at`; every reader — `list`, the producer, `suppress` consumers — goes through it, so expiry is never evaluated elsewhere.\n- **Inbox producer**: `reason: notice` items, delivered once per `(session, notice id, updated_at)`, rendered `[rebar inbox] notice <severity>: <message> (until <ends_at>) — rebar notice list`; the message is the operator's own title, length-capped at 200 chars. `notice_suppress` is read by the alert-ingestion child; this story only stores and displays it.\n\nPositive rationale: a typed field with one active-now function is the smallest design where expiry cannot drift between readers; reusing `session_log`'s carve-out sites means the sweep is mechanical and each site already has a test shape to extend; no new event type keeps older clones on the preserve-and-ignore path with nothing to ignore.\n\nCompatibility/rollback: purely additive nullable keys; an older binary reads a `notice` ticket as an unknown type string (it appears in that clone's `list` — benign, verified by a reducer test that an unrecognised type string reduces without error); rollback is deploying the older binary, no data migration.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/schemas/common.schema.json`, `ticket_state.schema.json`, `ticket_state_llm.schema.json`, `notice.schema.json` (new), `schemas/__init__.py`, `types.py` (regen), `docs/output-schemas.md`.\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`, `_processors_status.py`, `_state.py`, `_version.py`; `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py` (SNAPSHOT carry), `composer.py`, `composer_edit.py`, `notice.py` (new).\n- Carve-out sites listed above; `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/writes.py`, `_cli/_registry.py`; `_lib_writes.py`, `_lib_reads.py`, `__init__.py`; `_mcp_writes.py`, `_mcp_reads.py`, `_mcp_models.py`; `llm/plan_review/claimability.py`, `criteria_routing.json`.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/inbox.py` (producer), `docs/event-schema.md`, `docs/ticket-model.md` (regen via `scripts/gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py`), `docs/mcp-reference.md`, `docs/cli-reference.md`, `docs/config-reference.md` (regen), `docs/user-guide.md`, `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` (regen).\n- Tests: `tests/unit/reducer/test_notice_fold.py`, `tests/unit/test_notice_active.py`, `tests/interfaces/cli/test_notice_cli.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_notice.py`, compaction snapshot round-trip test.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Unit (pure): `active_notices` boundary matrix with an injected clock — `now == starts_at` active, `now == ends_at` inactive, cancelled (`ends_at = now`) inactive, window > 24h rejected at post; reducer fold/EDIT/SNAPSHOT round-trip; unknown-type-string tolerance.\n- CLI subprocess: `post` → `list` shows it; after `cancel`, `list` is empty while `list --all` shows it; exit codes; `--output json` validates.\n- MCP in-process: `post_notice` then any tool call from another session yields one `notice` inbox item; the same session's next call yields none (at-most-once); an expired notice yields nothing (contrast).\n- Carve-out regressions: `list`, `ready`, `next-batch` exclude the ticket; linking it with `blocks` is rejected; the reconciler outbound differ skips it (existing test shapes extended). Gate: `make test`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar notice post --until 2h \"Gerrit down\"` creates a ticket with `ticket_type == \"notice\"` and a 2h window, and `rebar notice list --output json` validates against `notice.schema.json`; verified by `tests/interfaces/cli/test_notice_cli.py`.\n- [ ] A notice is reported active at `starts_at` and inactive at `ends_at` and after `cancel`; a window longer than 24h is rejected with exit 1; verified by `tests/unit/test_notice_active.py`.\n- [ ] Every session receives each active notice exactly once via the inbox on MCP, CLI, and library seams; verified by `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_notice.py` and the CLI/library cases.\n- [ ] `list`, `ready`, and `next-batch` never return a `notice`; `blocks`/`depends_on` to a notice is rejected; the reconciler never emits one outbound; verified by the extended carve-out tests.\n- [ ] A CREATE with an unrecognised `ticket_type` string reduces without error and `KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES` is unchanged while `SCHEMA_VERSION == 6`; verified by `tests/unit/reducer/test_notice_fold.py`.\n- [ ] `docs/ticket-model.md` and `types.py` are regenerated and the generated-artifact drift gate passes; verified by `make test`.","id":"ac3a-9ea7-530d-48f4","parent_id":"44a9-92b4-831c-4a92","priority":2,"tags":["notifications","notice"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"notice ticket type: typed window fields, notice post/list/cancel/extend on three seams, active-notice inbox producer, suppress field"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788561032182075001,"uuid":"b571230f-6d36-415a-99ea-2150fdf7d1dc"}